<title>COLOMBIA: Colombia cuts internal coffee price by 2.5 percent.</title>
<headline>Colombia cuts internal coffee price by 2.5 percent.</headline>
<dateline>BOGOTA 1997-07-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Colombia cuts its internal coffee price by 2.5 percent Friday, setting it at 331,375 pesos per 125- kg load, the National Coffee Growers' Federation said.</p>
<p>It was the eighth price cut since Jan. 31, when a new sliding scale formula was introduced to adjust prices paid to growers on a weekly basis and allow them to better track world market prices.  </p>
<p>The latest price was based on an average price of $1.98 per pound in international markets. The previous price was set at 339,875 pesos per load.</p>
<p>((--Juan Guillermo Londono, Bogota newsroom, 571 610 7944))</p>
